====
---- QUERY
# A word ending an expression is not an alias: this is one row of two columns.
set planner=calcite;
set fallback_planner=none;
values((case when true then 1 else 2 end), (3));
---- RESULTS
1,3
---- TYPES
TINYINT, TINYINT
====
---- QUERY
# IMPALA-15681: Fix this test by creating a UDF function
# It should return a single row of two values. We know that
# it parses correctly because the second value "2" does not
# have any parens around it, but we get past the parsing stage
# and get an analysis error that the function doesn't exist.
set planner=calcite;
set fallback_planner=none;
values ((1+my_udf(1)), 2);
---- CATCH: ANY_OF
my_udf() unknown
No match found for function signature MY_UDF
====
